    {
      "id": "claim_a30602dced6a435e8fa1787403665d34",
      "statement": "For a bearer request the JWT filter checks blacklist status, then extracts email before calling `validateAccessToken`; it populates the Spring security context only when extraction yields an email and validation returns true, otherwise it continues the chain unauthenticated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://engine-spring-starter/src/main/java/com/engine/starter/security/JwtAuthenticationFilter.java#L32-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec74de188a6d4b932268a7271c65cd3cc34adfe2f1be826ec7942c1b4ac6851d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_caeae6b984f1426ca5de71d810a18ee7",
      "statement": "JWT validation deliberately catches parsing exceptions and returns `false`, but email extraction does not catch parsing exceptions; because extraction precedes validation in the filter, malformed bearer tokens can propagate instead of following the false-validation path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://engine-spring-starter/src/main/java/com/engine/starter/security/JwtAuthenticationFilter.java#L45-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed00898b139f712ce65d14c59abb7e3909f64b31716c74ba15fad7cc5e36acc9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://engine-spring-starter/src/main/java/com/engine/starter/security/JwtServiceAdapter.java#L48-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48686d32853199d7513cc970bcc5b113fc067849c74365952c64443e9ba65160:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_747dd4bb521148088b92b174e9a60c7b",
      "statement": "Controller-layer runtime exceptions are mapped to HTTP 400 with their message by `GlobalExceptionHandler`, while this handler does not convert filter-level parsing into boolean validation.",
